  "_comment": "Single source of truth for the engine <-> IB instrument map. Consumed by bridge/ib_bridge/instruments.py and web/lib/instruments.ts. direction_sign = +1 when the IB contract moves with the engine symbol, -1 when inverted (6J quotes JPY in USD while the engine tracks USDJPY). notation '32nds' means UST futures tick display; tick_fraction_of_32nd is the CME minimum tick expressed as a fraction of 1/32. Fields set to null are unknown/unverified on purpose - never guess them. key = stable lookup key (bridge /contracts/resolve?key=). role: primary = the instrument the desk trades for that engine symbol (FX ideas use spot on IDEALPRO), alternative = same engine view via another contract (FX futures), context = shown but not traded (DXY, HYG), curve = UST curve futures without their own engine view.",
